# The external client-facing JWT verification key used only by the
# proxyserver package's own tests (testdata/integration_test.cfg,
# testdata/orchestration_test.cfg, and several *_test.go files' inline
# config, all referencing it as ./public.pem relative to proxyserver/, the
# tests' working directory). mcp_client_test.go's init() generates a fresh
# RSA keypair every test run and writes only this public half here - the
# matching private key never touches disk at all. Not needed in
# production, which uses jwksUrl instead (see proxy-server.cfg).
/proxyserver/public.pem

# The LLM API key passed to ./scripts/deploy.sh --ai-api-key-file for
# ai-powered-tools (see docs/architecture/utility-and-ai-tools.md). Real, sensitive secret material —
# never committed.
/ai-api-key.txt

# A GitHub PAT for ./scripts/build.sh --release / ./scripts/deploy.sh
# --release's --github-token-file (see docs/architecture/build-deploy.md). Real, sensitive secret material — never committed.
/github-token.txt

# Secret material under common names, anywhere in the tree - so a key saved
# under a name of its own (e.g. an --ai-api-key-file ./openai-key.txt, a
# TLS key, an .env file) is never committed by a broad "git add".
*-key.txt
*token*.txt
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
.env
.env.*

# Incremental-build stamp files for the root Makefile's per-target
# staleness tracking (go list -deps-derived transitive dependencies — see
# Makefile, scripts/build.sh) — regenerated on every build, never committed.
/.build/

# CLI binaries built by ./scripts/build.sh (see scripts/cli.sh,
# go-gardening-demo/cli.sh) — local build artifacts, not committed.
/bin/
/go-gardening-demo/bin/

# Personal Claude Code settings/instructions — per-contributor, never committed.
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md

# Compiled binaries for every "package main" directory in this module.
# `go build ./...` run from the repo root drops one binary per main package
# here at the root (named after its directory); `go build .` run inside a
# package directory drops a same-named binary there. Both forms are listed.
# Root-level patterns are anchored with a leading "/" so they never match a
# same-named directory elsewhere. /claude-bridge, /cli and
# /demo-authorization-server are deliberately NOT listed: each collides
# with a real source directory at the root, and a pattern without a
# trailing slash would ignore that whole directory. `go build ./...` can't
# write a file over an existing directory anyway, so nothing is lost.
/go-proxy
/ai-powered-tools
/client
/gendata
/patchcfg
/garden-business-ops
/garden-customer-admin
/garden-customer-service
/garden-online-store
/garden-staff-admin
/declarative-guardrail
/event-aggregator
/rate-limiter
/driver
/generator
/ai-mcp-servers/ai-powered-tools/ai-powered-tools
/claude-bridge/claude-bridge
/cmd/go-proxy/go-proxy
/cli/cli
/demo-authorization-server/demo-authorization-server
/demo-authorization-server/client/client
/go-gardening-demo/cli/cli
/go-gardening-demo/gendata/gendata
/go-gardening-demo/patchcfg/patchcfg
/go-gardening-demo/servers/garden-business-ops/garden-business-ops
/go-gardening-demo/servers/garden-customer-admin/garden-customer-admin
/go-gardening-demo/servers/garden-customer-service/garden-customer-service
/go-gardening-demo/servers/garden-online-store/garden-online-store
/go-gardening-demo/servers/garden-staff-admin/garden-staff-admin
/platform-mcp-servers/declarative-guardrail/declarative-guardrail
/platform-mcp-servers/event-aggregator/event-aggregator
/platform-mcp-servers/rate-limiter/rate-limiter
/stress-test/driver/driver
/stress-test/generator/generator

